{
  "branch": "fixqa5",
  "status": "Stopped new work at the requested ten-minute-remaining cutoff. Changes left in fixqa5 working tree; no commit, push, deploy, docker, version, changelog or AGENTS changes.",
  "findings": {
    "R221": {
      "cause": "Bonfire phase freshness and display stage were page-local. Rejected shared-memory speech fell through to the remote queue. Queue completion was not immediately persisted, and startup restoration could copy an already queued cue.",
      "fix": "Per-account durable announcement keys cover Bonfire phases/stages/end, Halloween once cues and story fallback announcements. Shared-memory rejection is final. Save accepted queues and completions immediately; deduplicate restore; resume unfinished seasonal/story lines without re-running announcement guards. Revalidate phase/stage before delivery."
    },
    "R217": {
      "cause": "Ordinary pools contained only a few eligible responses; least-recent selection recycled them as soon as the short cooldown elapsed.",
      "fix": "Twelve new lines for each resident in each of morning/afternoon/evening, plus 28 conditional lines per resident. Conditions cover weekday, room, forecast, season, completed jobs, all six owned consoles and story chapter. A 24-hour shared-memory exclusion precedes selection; exhausted ambient pools stay quiet. Bonfire Talk also yields to normal fresh conversation after its seasonal explanation has been heard, while preserving the display interaction."
    },
    "R216": {
      "cause": "Every unfinished-job question returned the same chore.<job>.give recording.",
      "fix": "All fifteen jobs have alternative complete instructions and short reminders, selected through the shared picker. A heard introduction switches to reminders; after the short reminders are familiar, ordinary fresh conversation is allowed. Cat: four introductions and twelve brief reminders, with accurate bowl/call instructions."
    },
    "R219": {
      "cause": "The computer nag was chosen randomly without a PC-use condition; house moments also mistook H.stood for computer use. Conditions were checked only when a line was selected.",
      "fix": "Computer nags require monitor mode, and serialized context is checked again at delivery and after reload. Audited ambient gates cover next-day school, television power/text, actual ketchup placement, completed work before praise, and delayed loud-TV nags."
    },
    "R218": {
      "cause": "Talk selected an old line and silently discarded it afterwards; the Talk prompt remained unchanged.",
      "fix": "Choose fresh lines first. Exhaustion produces a silent animated nod/smile and brief bubble through the shared family queue. Prompts identify speaking, busy and listening; repeated F does not interrupt a sentence."
    },
    "R215": {
      "cause": "Engaging in conversation disabled the seated lap IK, allowing a standing talk-arm pose to fall into the armrest.",
      "fix": "Retain the seated thigh support. Keep one hand planted and allow only a small upward gesture with the other. The real rig is tested across all three residents and four seats."
    },
    "R220": {
      "cause": "dragTick immediately pulled the beanbag centre to the generic furniture reach, regardless of its pickup distance.",
      "fix": "For the beanbag only, store the original player-to-object offset in view coordinates and drag from that offset. Other furniture keeps its existing reach. The release threshold uses that actual radius too, so turning does not create a false caught release."
    }
  },
